.TH BIGFLOATSHIFTLEFT 3 "2026-09-22" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatShiftLeft, bigFloatShiftRight \- shift a binary big float mantissa
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatShiftLeft(BigFloat *" "x" ", int " "bits" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatShiftRight(BigFloat *" "x" ", int " "bits" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions shift the mantissa of x by bits positions, then normalize it.
Left shift multiplies the value by 2 raised to bits.
Right shift divides by that factor but discards low mantissa bits; it can
lose precision or become zero.  It is not just an exponent adjustment.
.PP
A zero count has no effect.  Negative counts delegate to the opposite integer
mantissa shift before normalization.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or the integer-shift or normalization error.
Errors leave x unchanged.  Exponent adjustment is checked for overflow.
.SH NOTES
The count handling and capacity limits in
.BR bigIntShiftLeft (3)
apply.  Left shift can fail when the shifted mantissa exceeds MAX_LIMBS,
even when the scaled value could be represented by changing only exp.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigFloatNormalize (3),
.BR bigIntShiftLeft (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
